==English==
{{was wotd|2012|March|4}}
[[File:Philtrum.jpg|thumb|the '''philtrum''']]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|filtrum}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*-trom}}
Borrowed from the {{bor|en|la|philtrum||a love potion}}, from {{bor|en|grc|φῐ́λτρον||a love charm; the dimple in the upper lip}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɪl.tɹəm/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-philtrum.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|philtra|s}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[shallow]] [[vertical]] [[groove]] running from the [[nasal septum]] to the center of the [[upper lip]].
#: {{syn|en|infranasal depression}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=[[w:M.L. Kulkarni|M. L. Kulkarni]]|title=Physical Examination of Children|series=Clinical Methods in Paediatrics|url=https://www.jaypeebrothers.com/pgDetails.aspx?cat=s&book_id=9788180612855|seriesvolume=2B|location=India|publisher=w:Jaypee Brothers|page=142|text=Oral intercommissural distance (mouth width) and '''philtrum''' length are useful measurements for diagnosis of wide or large mouth (macrostomia), small mouth (microstomia), long '''philtrum''' and short '''philtrum''' and form ‘good handles’ in syndromic delineation.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Loren J. Borud; Arin K. Greene|chapter=Chapter 24: Lip Reconstruction|editors=w:Josef E. Fischer; Kirby I. Bland; Mark P. Callery|title=Mastery of Surgery|url=https://books.google.com/books?&id=PgUFJg_-f4YC|volume=1|edition=5th|page=301|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?&id=PgUFJg_-f4YC&pg=PA301|column=3|text=Upper lip reconstruction is more difficult than lower lip reconstruction because the upper lip has a central structure, the '''philtrum'''.{{...}}Wounds adjacent to the '''philtrum''' that are closed primarily may shift the '''philtrum''' to the affected side. However, with time, the '''philtrum''' will tend to return to its midline position.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Hrishikesh Dubey|title=Mysteries of Vedic Face Reading|url=https://books.google.com/books?&id=cObWJt-CetAC|section=Categorization of the Philtrum According to Its Length|sectionurl=https://books.google.com/books?&id=cObWJt-CetAC&pg=PT166|text=If the '''philtrum''' is long and deep, then these people are very romantic, sexual, lively and friendly.}}
# {{lb|en|zootomy}} The [[junction]] between the two [[half|halves]] of an animal's [[upper lip]] or [[nose]].

